From 19b94adaad6a575c6147490177c16da34784d1df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:27:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(GPU): support devfreq-scaled GPUs that are not PCI
 devices

SoC GPUs are platform devices: the card has no PCI class, vendor or device
file, so get_gpu failed before it got anywhere and no GPU was exported on
arm64 handhelds.

Add a devfreq backend for them. A card without a PCI class file is handed
to it; it finds the devfreq node that scales the GPU (the card's own device
for panfrost/panthor/lima/etnaviv, or the Adreno node bound into msm's
display DRM device), identifies the GPU from its devicetree compatible
(vendor id is the PCI id Vulkan reports, e.g. 5143 for Qualcomm), and maps:

- ClockLimitMhzMin/Max   -> lowest/highest available_frequencies
- ClockValueMhzMin/Max   -> min_freq/max_freq (snapped to an OPP)
- ManualClock            -> narrows the governor's range; turning it off
                            restores the full range. Starts off: the range
                            sysfs reports includes thermal limits, so it
                            cannot tell a user's choice apart.
- class "integrated", no TDP interface.
